ta so we just constantly talk  back and forth and we just try to tie it  together this collaborative effort  extends beyond just the observers the  analysts and the players to include the  overwatch development team overwatch  league is built on a competitive  experience that continues to evolve it's  subject to constant tweaks the  introduction of new characters that  create entirely new gameplay dynamics  and the creation of new tools to improve  the spectating experience and bliss it  doesn't make these tweaks in isolation  it seeks out multiple perspectives to  best serve its casual players pro  players and viewers across a broad range  of experience levels what's up everyone  this is Jeff from the overwatch team it  relies on feedback from the massive  overwatch community expert analysts and  the production staff to shape all  aspects of the game and the league it's  actually really special how close  Blizzard and the development team from  overwatch is working  together with the Oval which leaked it  adds a lot they basically sit down and  try to be the viewer themselves like  what do they want to see from the game  and if they see something in the  interface for example like that that's a  bit confusing maybe there are too many  numbers they they then tweak it from  their own experience as a viewer so  they're really not just looking down at  things like they're there inside of the  whole thing which makes it very special  I think a big challenge of the overwatch  league is the fact that the game that's  being played is still being developed  and still evolving I don't look at it as  a problem I look at it as an opportunity  it's very cool to have the ability to  watch a stage of overwatch league and  talk about what should we iterate on and  have a community that's very open to us  making change for the better as long as  they believe that we're making those  changes for the better so when it comes  to adding new characters I know one way  to look at it is l